---
/**
 * /privacy-policy — how DAIT handles enquiry data.
 *
 * Written against what the site ACTUALLY does: the enquiry form posts the
 * standard lead payload to /api/leads (src/lib/leads.ts), which emails the
 * institute and files the contact in Brevo. Attribution comes from the
 * first-party sessionStorage/localStorage keys set in BaseLayout. If any of
 * that changes, update this page and /cookie-policy in the same commit.
 */
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config/site";

const centre = siteConfig.centers[0];
const address = [
  centre.name,
  ...centre.addressLines,
  `${centre.city}, ${centre.state}${centre.postalCode ? " " + centre.postalCode : ""}`,
].join(", ");
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How DAIT Institute collects, uses and protects the personal information you share through our enquiry forms, WhatsApp and website."
  canonicalPath="/privacy-policy/"
  updated="2026-09-23"
  intro="This policy explains what we collect when you enquire about a program, why we collect it, who we share it with, and the choices you have."
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This website is operated by <strong>{siteConfig.legalName}</strong> ("DAIT Institute", "we",
    "us"), an IT training institute based in {centre.city}, {centre.state}, India.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Address:</strong> {address}<br />
    <strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a><br />
    <strong>Phone:</strong> <a href={`tel:${siteConfig.phone.replace(/\s/g, "")}`}>{siteConfig.phone}</a>
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>

  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <p>
    When you submit an enquiry form, request a callback, or message us on WhatsApp, we collect:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your <strong>name</strong> and <strong>phone number</strong> (required, so an advisor can call you back)</li>
    <li>Your <strong>email address</strong> (optional)</li>
    <li>The <strong>program you're interested in</strong>, if you select one</li>
    <li>Whether you describe yourself as a <strong>graduate/student or a working professional</strong>, so we recommend the right track</li>
    <li>Any <strong>message</strong> you choose to write</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not ask for identity documents, financial details or payment information through this
    website. Please don't send those via the enquiry form or WhatsApp.
  </p>

  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <p>
    So we know which of our pages and campaigns actually help people find us, your browser stores a
    small amount of information on your own device and sends it along if you later submit an
    enquiry:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>The page you landed on and how many pages you viewed</li>
    <li>The website or search engine that referred you (for example Google, Facebook or WhatsApp)</li>
    <li>Campaign tags (UTM parameters) if you arrived from an advertisement or a link we shared</li>
    <li>How many times you have visited, and when you first visited</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The exact keys used are listed in our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a>. We also use
    Google Analytics to understand overall traffic patterns — that is covered there too.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>To respond to your enquiry</strong> — a counselling call, course details, batch timings and fees</li>
    <li><strong>To recommend the right program</strong> for your background and goals</li>
    <li><strong>To send you information you asked for</strong>, such as a curriculum or admission details</li>
    <li><strong>To improve the website</strong> — understanding which pages and programs people look for</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We process this information on the basis of your consent, given when you submit a form or
    message us. You can withdraw that consent at any time (see <a href="#your-rights">Your rights</a>).
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>We do not sell your personal information</strong>, and we do not share it with other
    institutes or training providers.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We share information only with the service providers that help us run the website and respond
    to enquiries:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Brevo</strong> — stores your enquiry in our contact records and sends our
      notification and response emails. Brevo is based in the European Union.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google</strong> — Google Analytics and Google Tag Manager, for website traffic
      measurement.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Meta (WhatsApp, and Facebook/Instagram advertising)</strong> — if you contact us on
      WhatsApp, that conversation happens on Meta's platform under Meta's own privacy terms. If we
      are running advertising, a Meta advertising pixel may also be active.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Vercel</strong> — hosts this website and serves its pages.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some of these providers operate outside India, which means your information may be processed
    abroad. We share only what is needed for the purpose described above.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may also disclose information where the law requires it, or to establish or defend a legal
    claim.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep enquiry records for as long as needed to respond and to maintain our admissions
    records — normally up to <strong>three years</strong> from your last contact with us, unless
    you ask us to delete them sooner or we are required to keep them longer. Analytics data is
    retained according to the settings in Google Analytics.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, you can ask us to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal information we hold about you</li>
    <li><strong>Correct</strong> anything that is inaccurate or incomplete</li>
    <li><strong>Delete</strong> your information, where we have no continuing need for it</li>
    <li><strong>Withdraw your consent</strong> and stop receiving calls or messages from us</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To do any of these, email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a> from the
    address you contacted us with, or call <a href={`tel:${siteConfig.phone.replace(/\s/g, "")}`}>{siteConfig.phone}</a>.
    We will respond as quickly as we can, and in any case within the timelines the law requires.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are not satisfied with how we have handled your request, you may raise a grievance with
    us at the same address, and you have the right to complain to the Data Protection Board of
    India.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiries are submitted over an encrypted (HTTPS) connection and stored with the providers
    listed above. We limit access to enquiry records to the people who need it to contact you. No
    system is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security, but we take these
    safeguards seriously.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Our programs are intended for adults and for students at or above college entry age. We do not
    knowingly collect personal information from children under 18 without the consent of a parent
    or guardian. If you believe a child has submitted information to us, contact us and we will
    delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we change how we handle personal information, we will update this page and change the "last
    updated" date above.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
